        "faq_9XmEpe": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>What Book Should a Two-Year-Old Read?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Early learning books for 2-year-olds should be fun, colorful, and teach basic ideas like numbers, letters, and simple phrases. Tuttle Toddlers books are a fantastic choice because of their enjoyable and interactive stories.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_49jae6": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>What Age Range Are Toddler Books For?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Toddler books are for children between the ages of 1 and 4. These books are all about helping your toddler learn basic skills like counting, reading, and learning about the world in ways that are easy to understand.</p><p>Tuttle Toddlers books are ideal early learning books for 3-year-olds.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_D74DWn": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Can a Child Start Reading At 2?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>At age 2, most kids can't read on their own, but they can start learning the fundamentals of reading, such as how to recognize letters, sounds, and words. Our books teach these ideas in a fun and easy-to-understand style, which will encourage your child to learn to read and write early on.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_YprrPc": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>How Much Time Does Each Lesson Take?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Each book in our preschool homeschool curriculum is designed to take about 20–30 minutes to read. However, this can be extended or reduced based on your child’s interest and attention span, allowing you to adapt each lesson to fit your schedule.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_R46rtA": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Can I Use This Curriculum Alongside Other Educational Materials?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Absolutely! Our preschool homeschool curriculum is flexible and can be used alongside other resources. Our books are a great addition to any learning plan and can be used with additional reading materials.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_nwmmAD": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Can You Use Tuttle Twins Books for Homeschooling?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, our educational kids' books are perfect for homeschooling families. They cover a wide range of topics, like <a href=\"https://www.tuttletwins.com/products/the-tuttle-toddlers-abcs-of-liberty\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Liberty</span></a> and <a href=\"https://www.tuttletwins.com/products/the-tuttle-toddlers-abcs-of-economics\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Economics</span></a>, that can complement your curriculum, making learning both enjoyable and effective.0</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        }
